// RUF005(n): findings from clauses `collection-literal-concatenation`, `collection-literal-concatenation-in-string-type`, which say the same.
// Each rule is one way a JSON `rule` can match.
// Columns after `at` are the metavariables the JSON's message, anchor or `each` names: one finding per distinct row.
.violation RUF005(at: node, e: node) "Write one literal with unpacking, such as `[*a, 1, *b]` or `(*a, 1)`, instead of adding collections with `+`. Keep `+` if an operand defines its own `__add__`."
    suppress noqa "RUF005"
RUF005(E, n) :- !ruf005_alt_6(n), child(n, c1, _), ruf005_outer_operand(c1, E).
RUF005(E, n) :- ruf005_type_string(n, E).

